diff --git a/docs/CHANGELOG.md b/docs/CHANGELOG.md
index 8440eb4..84c9c03 100644
--- a/docs/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/docs/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -4,6 +4,12 @@ Notable project changes are recorded here. GitHub Release pages remain the sourc
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Keep Loaded now retains local models under ordinary RAM pressure and preloads downloaded default models in the background when memory allows. Recovery requires stable memory headroom and a retry cooldown; critical RAM/GPU pressure still reclaims idle models. Other memory policies retain their one-minute recent-use grace period. Browser development sessions reject interrupted response bodies instead of passing null into model settings.
+
+- Fidelity Windows launches can handle Ctrl+Win single-tap hands-free directly, without a separate key-injection helper. Either press order and staggered modifier presses work; a short release enables hands-free, the next chord stops it, and holding the complete chord for 350 ms preserves hold-to-talk.
+
+- Local Light cleanup now validates exact wording before accepting model or cached output. Clear formatting cues, identifier underscores, and bounded weekday corrections are handled deterministically; unsupported edits preserve the transcript without retrying or escalating models. Windows model launches also suppress console creation without changing installed runtime binaries.
+
 - Added desktop-only Paste in Chunks in Context Advanced settings. It inserts small pieces with pauses for CLI prompts, preserves the clipboard, and stops remaining chunks when focus or clipboard ownership changes.
 
 - Fixed Linux shortcut capture rejecting Ctrl + Super when the WebView reports Super as an OS key.
diff --git a/docs/CLEANUP_LEVELS.md b/docs/CLEANUP_LEVELS.md
index 3d24955..8bc1c14 100644
--- a/docs/CLEANUP_LEVELS.md
+++ b/docs/CLEANUP_LEVELS.md
@@ -13,6 +13,27 @@ After transcription, Verenu can run the raw text through an LLM cleanup step bef
 
 Use **Off** when you need the raw model output. **Light** is useful when wording and structure should remain close to what you said. **Medium** is the default for everyday dictation. **Strong** is for concise output when the important details still need to remain intact.
 
+### Local Light cleanup
+
+Local Light cleanup preserves the recognized words and their order. It handles a
+limited set of clear spoken punctuation cues, scoped identifier underscores,
+accidental article repetitions, and explicit weekday corrections before asking
+the selected local model to adjust punctuation and capitalization. Literal text,
+snippet expansions, technical tokens, and configured vocabulary are protected.
+Ambiguous wording stays unchanged.
+
+Model results and cached text must preserve that prepared transcript. An
+unsupported edit, failed request, or truncated completion uses the prepared
+transcript immediately, without another cleanup attempt or automatic escalation
+to a different model. Medium and Strong retain their existing behavior.
+
+English-specific rules require an explicitly English transcription language.
+Local Light validates against the primary transcript; alternate-only wording is
+not automatically accepted as a correction. Saved instructions can still apply
+supported deterministic formatting, but requests for rewriting do not override
+word preservation. Prompt audits measure the model response separately from the
+pipeline's fallback protection.
+
 ## Changing it
 
 - **During setup**: choose the default cleanup level in the first-run setup.
